===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leyp-}}
{{ety|en|id=be alive|:inh|enm:lefe}}
From {{inh|en|enm|lefe}}, {{m|enm|lifen}}, {{m|enm|libbe}}, {{m|enm|libben}}, {{m|enm|live}}, {{m|enm|luvien}}, {{m|enm|lyven}}, from {{inh|en|ang|libban}}, {{m|ang|lifian|t=to live; be alive}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*libbjan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*libjaną|t=to live}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leyp-|t=to stick}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|yol|live|t=to live}}, {{cog|frr|laawe}}, {{m|frr|lawe}}, {{m|frr|lewe}}, {{m|frr|lewi}}, {{m|frr|lewwe}}, {{m|frr|lääwe|t=to live}}, {{cog|stq|lieuwje}}, {{m|stq|líeuwje|t=to live}}, {{cog|fy|libje|t=to live}}, {{cog|gsw|läbe|t=to live}}, {{cog|cim,mhn|lem|t=to live}}, {{cog|nl|leeven}}, {{m|nl|leven|t=to live}}, {{cog|de|leben|t=to live}}, {{cog|nds-de|lęven|t=to live}}, {{cog|li|leve}}, {{m|li|léëve|t=to live}}, {{cog|lb|liewen|t=to live}}, {{cog|wym|łaowa|t=to live}}, {{cog|yi|לעבן|t=to live}}, {{cog|da,nb|leve|t=to live}}, {{cog|fo|liva|t=to live}}, {{cog|is|lifa|t=to live}}, {{cog|nn|leva}}, {{m|nn|leve}}, {{m|nn|liva|t=to live}}, {{cog|sv|leva|t=to live}}, {{cog|got|𐌻𐌹𐌱𐌰𐌽|t=to live}}; also {{cog|la|lippus|t=half-sighted, myopic}}, {{cog|el|λίπος|t=fat, tallow}}, {{cog|lt|lipti|t=to stick}}, {{cog|bg|лепя́|t=to glue, paste, stick; to plaster, smear}}, {{cog|cs|lepit|t=to glue, stick}}, {{cog|mk|лепи|t=to glue, stick}}, {{cog|pl|lepić|t=to mold; to glue, paste; to stick}}, {{cog|ru|лепи́ть|t=to fashion, sculpt, shape}}, {{cog|sh|лепити}}, {{m|sh|лије́пити}}, {{m|sh|lépiti}}, {{m|sh|lijépiti|t=to glue, paste; to stick}}, {{cog|sk|lepiť|t=to stick}}, {{cog|sl|lepiti|t=to stick}}, {{cog|uk|ліпити|t=to mould, shape}}, {{cog|sa|लिप्|t=to anoint, smear; to defile, soil, taint}}, {{m|sa|रिप्|t=deceit, fraud; injury; enemy, traitor}}.
